title: Run acp-tck as a tackle conformance check — tasks
status: draft
created: 2026-10-24
author: adrian
items[14]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,[x] Pinned acp-tck toolchain,"Add agentclientprotocol/acp-tck as a nix flake input in nix/flake.nix and package it with uv2nix so its Python environment resolves from the repository's committed uv.lock. Merge the package into the default dev shell and confirm the acp-tck CLI resolves; update nix/flake.lock.","Inside nix develop acp-tck --version prints the pinned version; the flake evaluates and nix flake show succeeds; flake.lock records the acp-tck revision; running acp-tck needs no network access.",high,"3-5h",,"pinned-tck-toolchain,hermetic-pinning"
  T-002,[x] Test model bin scaffold,"Add src/bin/tackle-test-model.rs to agentkit-tackle with an axum server and clap CLI: --bind (default 127.0.0.1) and --port plus --cancel-sentinel. Register the bin target in Cargo.toml beside tackle-mcp-echo. The process binds localhost only and writes diagnostics to stderr.","cargo build -p agentkit-tackle --bin tackle-test-model succeeds; the binary starts, binds the given address, logs to stderr, and exits cleanly on SIGTERM; release and nix packaging do not include the bin.",low,"1-2h",,"deterministic-test-model,no-product-cost"
  T-003,Deterministic streaming completions,"Implement POST /v1/chat/completions in tackle-test-model: parse the request, derive the reply text and finish_reason solely from the request body, and stream an OpenAI-compatible SSE response with data deltas, a terminal usage chunk, and a non-streaming JSON shape when the request sets stream to false. No randomness, no clocks, no outbound network.","A request with a known body yields byte-identical streamed output across runs; the text and tool-call shapes the tackle provider parses are reproduced; a unit test asserts the SSE framing and the absence of outbound connections.",medium,"3-4h",T-002,"deterministic-test-model,offline-determinism"
  T-004,Cancel sentinel held stream,"When a request contains the value passed to --cancel-sentinel, respond with headers and one initial SSE chunk then hold the connection open emitting nothing until the client disconnects or a bounded timeout elapses, keeping a tackle turn in flight so acp-tck cancellation tests exercise session/cancel.","A sentinel request holds the stream open and is observed as not completed; cancelling the client closes the held stream promptly; a non-sentinel request is unaffected.",medium,"2-3h",T-003,"cancellation-exercise,cancellation-exercised"
  T-005,Test model tests,"Add offline tests for tackle-test-model: the streaming reply shape for a normal request, the non-streaming reply, the held-open sentinel, and prompt cancellation. Keep them network-free.","cargo test -p agentkit-tackle test_model passes offline; the sentinel test asserts the stream stays open until cancellation; no test touches the network.",medium,"2-3h","T-003,T-004","deterministic-test-model,cancellation-exercise,offline-determinism"
  T-006,Conformance config fixture,"Commit a tackle configuration fixture under crates/agentkit-tackle/tests/conformance/ whose endpoint base_url targets the test model's fixed localhost port with auth none and a model whose context window is known so usage reporting is live; it is passed via --config-dir by the runner.","Pointing the tackle binary at the fixture with --config-dir resolves a model and a context window; a session/prompt against the running test model returns end_turn; the fixture contains no secrets and no paths outside the repo.",low,"1-2h",T-003,"tackle-config-fixture"
  T-007,Runner recipes and orchestration,"Add crates/agentkit-tackle/mod.just with recipes to build the tackle and test model binaries, start the endpoint and record its pid, run the pinned acp-tck with --protocol-version 1 and explicit timeouts and --cancel-prompt set to the sentinel and --report-json to target/ and the tackle command 'agentkit-tackle stdio --config-dir <fixture>' after --, stop the endpoint, and one orchestration recipe that invokes them in order. Reference the crate as a module from the root justfile.","just tackle conformance runs end to end from a clean checkout inside nix develop, offline, and writes the JSON report; the orchestration recipe is the only entry point used by CI; discrete recipes run individually.",high,"4-6h","T-001,T-005,T-006","conformance-run,runner-owns-the-endpoint,local-parity,bounded-runtime"
  T-008,Port handling and cleanup,"Make the runner fail fast with a precise error naming the port when the test model address is already bound, and guarantee the endpoint is stopped on every exit path so no orphan process survives a failed or interrupted run.","Starting the orchestration recipe with the port pre-bound fails immediately naming the port and does not hang; after passing, failing, and interrupted runs no test model process remains.",low,"1-2h",T-007,"endpoint-port-unavailable,bounded-runtime"
  T-009,Baseline checker,"Add a stdlib python3 script under crates/agentkit-tackle/tests/conformance/ that reads the acp-tck JSON report, extracts every MANDATORY requirement whose status is not PASS, and diffs that set against the committed baseline. Exit non-zero only when a MANDATORY failure is absent from the baseline; report baseline ids that now pass and ids no longer present as drift; error with seeding guidance when the baseline file is absent. Never delete the report.","Given sample reports the checker exits zero for known failures, non-zero for a new MANDATORY failure, prints drift without failing, and errors clearly when the baseline is missing; it depends only on the python3 standard library.",medium,"3-4h",,"baseline-diff,report-artifact,baseline-absent,requirement-set-changes"
  T-010,Baseline checker tests,"Add fixture-driven tests for the checker: known failure tolerated, new MANDATORY failure detected, a NOT CONFORMANT verdict alone not failing, a now-passing baseline id reported as drift, a stale baseline id reported and tolerated, and a missing baseline erroring. Include a report fixture generated by a real acp-tck run.","The tests run offline in CI and cover every branch above; the checker's exit codes are asserted directly.",medium,"2-3h",T-009,"baseline-diff,baseline-drift-reported,new-failure-detected,baseline-absent,requirement-set-changes"
  T-011,Seed the committed baseline,"Run the orchestration recipe once against current tackle, review the MANDATORY failures, and commit them as the initial baseline file with a short comment that entries are known gaps to be burned down.","The baseline file exists and is committed; a second orchestration run passes the baseline diff; every baseline id is a real MANDATORY requirement id from the report.",low,"1-2h","T-007,T-009","baseline-diff,conformance-run-completes"
  T-012,Non-blocking CI job,"Add a reusable workflow (workflow_call) that runs just tackle conformance inside nix develop with continue-on-error, always uploads the JSON report as an artifact, and is invoked from pull-request.yaml on changes touching the tackle crate or the conformance inputs.","The workflow passes actionlint and zizmor; a deliberately failing run still uploads the report and does not fail the pull request's required checks or the merge queue; the job does not run for unrelated changes.",medium,"2-4h",T-011,"non-blocking-ci,report-artifact,ci-non-blocking,non-interference"
  T-013,Document the conformance posture,"Add a short conformance section to docs/docs/dev/tackle/protocol.mdx: what acp-tck covers, that the check is non-blocking and baselined, how to run it locally, and that the in-repo golden-transcript suite remains the fast check.","The docs build succeeds; the page names the orchestration recipe and the baseline; no claim of full conformance is made.",low,"1-2h",T-007,"transcript-suite-retained,non-blocking-ci"
  T-014,End-to-end verification,"Verify the whole feature: run the orchestration recipe with network disabled; run it twice and compare requirement statuses; run cargo test to confirm the golden-transcript suite still passes untouched; and confirm no release or nix artifact includes tackle-test-model.","The run completes with network disabled; two consecutive runs produce identical requirement statuses; cargo test -p agentkit-tackle passes with acp_v1_conformance present; nix and goreleaser outputs contain only the tackle binary.",medium,"2-3h","T-012,T-013","offline-run,deterministic-across-runs,transcript-suite-intact,no-product-cost"
